The rule as written says the check's answer ought to move between these two texts. The kernel conformance.kernel.recovered-from-prose is defined as: "Whether the harness had to recover the object from prose or a fence (yes) or read it as strict JSON (no)." The input is strict JSON, so the harness reads it as strict JSON and the answer is no. The rewritten text has the same object embedded in prose, so the harness has to recover it from prose and the answer is yes. Therefore the check's answer moves.